WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.650
Teacher midterm practice for C plus plus, question 31.

2
00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:08.125
Part two must use the fact that a double no longer

3
00:00:08.125 --> 00:00:11.494
changes when multiplied by ten once it is too large.

4
00:00:11.494 --> 00:00:15.206
Which test prints double out of range at the right moment?

5
00:00:16.905 --> 00:00:20.695
For every finite positive x, ten x is bigger than x.

6
00:00:20.695 --> 00:00:24.907
So x times ten equals x is false, and the loop keeps going.

7
00:00:25.528 --> 00:00:29.648
Once x has overflowed to inf, inf times ten is still inf.

8
00:00:29.648 --> 00:00:33.767
Now x times ten equals x is true, and the message prints.

9
00:00:35.366 --> 00:00:39.676
The theory: floating point overflow does not wrap like integers.

10
00:00:39.676 --> 00:00:44.962
It saturates at infinity, and infinity times anything positive is still infinity.

11
00:00:46.563 --> 00:00:49.634
So the test is: if x times ten equals x.

12
00:00:50.454 --> 00:00:55.482
Thinking floating point overflow wraps around like integers. It saturates at inf.

13
00:00:56.202 --> 00:01:00.739
Exam tip: try each candidate test on an ordinary value first.

14
00:01:00.739 --> 00:01:03.511
x times ten greater than x is true for every

15
00:01:03.511 --> 00:01:07.103
finite x, so that test would fire immediately.
